## Approach
In a circular houses, One thing to notice is if we are taking 0th index, then last index shouldnt be taken, likewise if last index is taken, 0th shouldnt be. This much we know.
So, We need two solutions, one is without the first element, and other is without the last and get the max of both.

In this space optimized approach, passing 1 as start for without first element ( 0th index ) and end is < n

passing 0 as start for without last element ( n-1 th index) end is < n-1

That's it. We know the remaining private helper function which is the space optimizated version.
#

## Solution
```cpp[]
class Solution {
private:
    int spaceOptimized(vector<int> &arr, int start, int n){

        int secprev = arr[start];
        int prev = max(arr[start], arr[start+1]);

        for(int i=start+2;i<n;i++){
            int pick = arr[i] + secprev;
            int dont = prev;

            int curr = max(pick, dont);

            secprev = prev;
            prev = curr;
        }
        return prev;
    }
public:
    int houseRobber(vector<int>& money) {
        int n = money.size();

        if(n==0) return 0;
        if(n==1) return money[0];

        int withoutFirst = spaceOptimized(money, 1, n);

        int withoutLast = spaceOptimized(money, 0, n-1);

        return max(withoutFirst, withoutLast);
    }
};
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
O(N)

**Space Complexity:**
O(1), not using any extra space for vectors , just some variables

